SWEET WLAN keep (patch 0268, sprint-wifi 2026-11-08, boot arg sweetwlankeep=1 together with sweetwlan=26; without the boot arg every path is the behaviour of patches 0174..0267 unchanged): after a finished L26 (WLC ping 10/10) the one-shot G2 hook no longer tears the link down. Today swg_go runs swg_undo (PCIe 0xC34 := 0, EP Command := 0x2 = bus master OFF, RC Command restored), the hook puts cfg 0x80 back, disarms the L25 store judge and sets h->g2 = 0, and W17 re-halts the CA7 and SYS_MEM wrapper (RESET_CTL := 1): the firmware dies seconds after it joined. With the boot arg: sweet_wlan_g2.h (patch 0174 copy, regenerated) skips the undo and the cfg 0x84 := 0 and sets x->kept (printed: `G2 keep: dongle left running`, a WIFI GAP naming what is not restored); the hook keeps h->g2 = 1 (the data path's host/DATA/doorbell stores exist only in sw3_wr's g2 branch and are judged by the L25 whitelist, which stays armed with h->l25w intact), leaves cfg 0x80 on the PCIe window the last doorbell used (sw_g2_bar0 moves it only on a difference, the list entry is repeatable), wipes the PMK copy, keeps bus and engine state static, and tells W17 (struct swl_wx keep) to skip the CA7/SM/ATU2/cfg 0x88 restore rows and the halt judgement (GAP instead of the STOP). The Apple en0 ifnet is then built over the live engine (new bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_en0_bus.h = shim/wlan_en0_bus.h, host-tested) by a kernel thread that waits for sweet_wlan_init to return, hands over with en0_live_up (engine quiet mode, boot address pixos_en0_ip through the existing sweet_wlan_en0_apply, now exported) and polls every 5 ms: ring 2 is read, printed as a WIFI GAP per unhandled item (events, DS_ENTER_REQ not acked, others) and consumed with the existing D2H-RD slot + doorbell pair, then rings 3/4 and the link watch; a stop of the engine ends the thread with no further store. One recursive mutex serialises that thread against the stack's transmit (EN0_LOCK in wlan_en0.h en0_output, patch 0199 regenerated). No new store kind: host-memory ring/index/payload stores and PCIe doorbell 0 only, all through the existing DP15 executor and the L25 judge. Not run on hardware. W-UI (sprint 2026-11-08, same patch): the kept link is made visible to iOS. (1) After en0_live_up the poll thread installs the Apple80211 handler on en0 with sweet_wlan_a80211_radio_attach_kept (patch 0201; the keep hand-over had no call to sweet_wlan_a80211_radio_attach, so wifid's SIOCGA80211 reached en0's own `ioctl unsupported`); a failure is a WIFI GAP. (2) The SSID, BSSID, channel and RSSI the FIRMWARE reports after L26 (sweet_wlan_l25_hs.h swl25_live) are copied by sw_keep_capture in the G2 hook and handed to that radio backend (kept link: Get 1/9/4/16/103/21 answer joined, same-SSID join succeeds, other join/leave/power off refused with a GAP; read once at the hand-over, not refreshed, a GAP says so); the record is wiped after the hand-over. (3) sweet_wlan_registry_set_bsd_name (patch 0200) puts `BSD Name` (kIOBSDNameKey), IOPrimaryInterface, IOBuiltin and IOLocation on the published SweetWLANInterface. No new hardware access: host memory and registry only.
